# Auto-run commands

When the user asks you to implement, fix, test, or run something:

- Run terminal commands yourself instead of only suggesting them.
- Do not wait for the user to run commands manually unless a command is destructive or needs explicit approval.
- After code changes, run relevant checks (e.g. `flutter analyze`, `dart analyze`) when useful.
- If `flutter run` is already active, prefer hot restart when a full restart is needed for asset or config changes.

This project uses Flutter on Windows. Flutter is at `C:\flutter\bin`.
